cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CS2RB, please cite the paper and the data archive."
type: dataset
title: "CS2RB: Aggregate and Individual-Player Models for Round-Win Prediction in Counter-Strike 2"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
authors:
  - family-names: Bishop
    given-names: William
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22970589"
    description: "CS2RB v1.0 data archive"
repository-code: "https://github.com/williambishop-research/cs2rb"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - Counter-Strike 2
  - esports analytics
  - win probability
  - set models
  - training-data scale
abstract: >-
  CS2RB v1.0 contains 4,768,984 live in-round game states from 12,742
  professional Counter-Strike 2 map recordings (5,725 matches, January-August
  2026, seven maps), with frozen chronological splits, and a fixed 336-fit
  protocol comparing aggregate models (XGBoost, MLP) with individual-player set
  models (Deep Sets, Set Transformer) across nested training scales.
